Kth Smallest Element in a BST- LeetCode 230
Today’s problem focused on finding the Kth smallest value in a Binary Search Tree (BST).
- Approach:
The key observation is that inorder traversal of a BST visits nodes in sorted ascending order.
So, I used the following approach:
Traverse the left subtree first.
Visit the current node and increment a count.
When count == k, the current node contains the Kth smallest element.
If k hasn't been reached, continue with the right subtree.
This makes the problem much simpler once we recognize the sorted-order property of BSTs.

-Time Complexity: O(n) :worst case, we may visit every node.
-Space Complexity: O(h): recursion stack, where h is the height of the tree.
